10:46:17 | INFO | 🤖 Target: That makes sense—if your alerts have consistently been confirmed malware, quarantine can feel unnecessary. But antivirus products are designed for all users and all kinds of detections, including uncertain ones. A file can be flagged because it is definitely known malware, because it behaves suspiciously, or because it resembles malware. Quarantine handles all of those cases safely: it immediately prevents the file from running, while avoiding irreversible deletion if the alert is mistaken or the file is needed for analysis. For a confirmed virus on a personal computer, deleting it from quarantine is usually the appropriate next step after the antivirus has finished cleaning related components.
